window.SEARCH_INDEX=[{"u":"locations/moosewood/","n":"Moosewood","t":"Locations","h":"moosewood locations the starting village and the only place in the game you are handed anything. everything an account needs in its first hour is inside a thirty-second walk of the dock: a tutorial npc, a rod shop, a fish buyer, a boat seller and the appraiser. stage 0 — start access spawn point key npcs pierre, marc, the merchant, the shipwright, the appraiser shop rods plastic, carbon, fast, lucky first boat rowboat, 400 c$"},{"u":"locations/the-ocean/","n":"The Ocean","t":"Locations","h":"the ocean locations the water between the islands is its own fishing location with its own bestiary, and it is where island names first appear on your screen — sail far enough from shore and the map fills itself in. unlocking a location in fisch mostly means visiting it once. stage 1 — early access any boat holds ocean-only bestiary, drifting hunt events danger deep water species outweigh early rods"},{"u":"locations/roslit-bay/","n":"Roslit Bay","t":"Locations","h":"roslit bay locations the second town, and the one that turns a beginner into a player. its blacksmith sells the steady rod, its shallows are a workable enchant relic farm, and its volcano is the first place the game refuses to let you fish without the right gear. stage 1 — early access sail from moosewood shop rod steady rod — 7,000 c$ notable roslit volcano; nurse shark shallows farms enchant relics"},{"u":"locations/terrapin-island/","n":"Terrapin Island","t":"Locations","h":"terrapin island locations an early island whose value is almost entirely bestiary. guides that route players to the 70% destiny rod gate name the same four blocks every time — moosewood, roslit bay, terrapin and the ocean — because they are large, easy and finishable with a rod you already own. stage 1 — early access sail best for bestiary completion difficulty low — early rods handle it"},{"u":"locations/sunstone-island/","n":"Sunstone Island","t":"Locations","h":"sunstone island locations one of the early-mid islands on the standard sailing loop. community sources are consistent that it exists and is worth a bestiary pass, and inconsistent about its shop stock from patch to patch — check the merchant when you land rather than trusting any list, this one included. stage 2 — early-mid access sail best for bestiary, mid-tier sell values"},{"u":"locations/snowcap-island/","n":"Snowcap Island","t":"Locations","h":"snowcap island locations cold-water fishing. its species do not appear in the southern islands, so it is a required stop for bestiary completion, and its weather is what makes the sleet mutation reachable. stage 2 — early-mid access sail north weather cold; snow conditions mutation sleet is a cold-biome mutation"},{"u":"locations/mushgrove-swamp/","n":"Mushgrove Swamp","t":"Locations","h":"mushgrove swamp locations the single best-value stop in the early-mid game, because the reward here is free. agaric asks you to catch an alligator in the swamp and hands over the fungal rod for nothing. stage 2 — early-mid access sail key npc agaric free rod fungal rod — catch an alligator species swamp-only bestiary"},{"u":"locations/forsaken-shores/","n":"Forsaken Shores","t":"Locations","h":"forsaken shores locations for most of the mid-game this is the answer to both “where do i make money” and “where do i level”, which is rare — usually those are different places. the waterfall pond is the specific spot guides point at. stage 3 — mid access sail; bring a real boat best for c$ per hour and xp per hour landmark waterfall pond, around −2685, 165, 1770 realistic rate 100k–500k c$/hr with a mid rod"},{"u":"locations/statue-of-sovereignty/","n":"Statue of Sovereignty","t":"Locations","h":"statue of sovereignty locations the island is a landmark; the reason you come is underneath it. go into the mines, find the npc standing next to the elevator, pay him 400 c$, and the elevator takes you down to the keepers altar — where every enchant in the game is applied. stage 3 — mid access sail gate bribe the npc by the mine elevator — 400 c$ leads to keepers altar"},{"u":"locations/keepers-altar/","n":"Keepers Altar","t":"Locations","h":"keepers altar locations the chamber beneath the statue of sovereignty where you trade an enchant relic for a random enchant on your rod. every rod in your endgame kit gets its power here, not in a shop. stage 3 — mid access under the statue of sovereignty cost to enter 400 c$ bribe, one time timing offer relics at night consumes enchant relics and exalted relics"},{"u":"locations/ancient-isle/","n":"Ancient Isle","t":"Locations","h":"ancient isle locations when players compare relic farms head to head, ancient isle comes out ahead of the roslit bay shallows. if you are building an enchant stack rather than hoping for one, this is the island you park on. stage 4 — mid-late access sail best for enchant relics compared with roslit bay — better here, per player testing"},{"u":"locations/northern-expedition/","n":"Northern Expedition &amp; Northern Summit","t":"Locations","h":"northern expedition & northern summit locations the far-north block. progression guides route through it for one reason: the arctic rod at northern summit is the standard buy between the free fungal rod and the trident rod, and it is the rod that makes the cold biomes comfortable. stage 4 — mid-late access sail north; cold water shop rod arctic rod, at the summit species arctic bestiary"},{"u":"locations/tridents-temple/","n":"Trident&#8217;s Temple","t":"Locations","h":"trident’s temple locations you come here to buy one thing. the trident rod is the most flexible mid-game rod in the game and its passive — a roughly 30% chance to apply the atlantean mutation, tripling a catch’s value — means it partly pays for itself. stage 4 — mid-late access sail shop rod trident rod — 150,000 c$ why atlantean mutation passive"},{"u":"locations/vertigo/","n":"Vertigo","t":"Locations","h":"vertigo locations a deep, dark, hostile zone, and the only door to the depths. it is also the first place the game asks for real completion rather than attendance: you need the whole vertigo bestiary before the key can drop. stage 5 — late access sail to deep water gate out 100% vertigo bestiary, then fish the strange whirlpool for the depths key danger heavy species; weak rods simply lose"},{"u":"locations/the-depths/","n":"The Depths","t":"Locations","h":"the depths locations a secret zone under vertigo that cannot be sailed to. inside is the rod of the depths at 750,000 c$ — the rod that carries most accounts from the late game into the endgame, and the reason people grind the vertigo bestiary at all. stage 5 — late access the depths key shop rod rod of the depths — 750,000 c$ prerequisite 100% vertigo bestiary"},{"u":"locations/atlantis/","n":"Atlantis","t":"Locations","h":"atlantis locations the sunken city, and the first location that gates on your character level rather than your boat. its rod is a genuine endgame item and its boss sits behind a five-lever world quest that most players do with a guide open. stage 6 — endgame access late-game sail; deep water shop rod kraken rod — 950,000 or 1,333,333 c$ level gate ~level 180 boss the kraken, in the kraken pool"},{"u":"locations/the-arch/","n":"The Arch","t":"Locations","h":"the arch locations the payoff for every easy bestiary entry you filled on the way here. at 70% total bestiary, caleia will sell you the destiny rod for 190,000 c$ — cheap for what it is, and the clearest example in fisch of collection work converting into gear. stage 6 — endgame access sail key npc caleia sells destiny rod — 190,000 c$ gate 70% total bestiary completion"},{"u":"locations/cursed-isle/","n":"Cursed Isle","t":"Locations","h":"cursed isle locations cursed water, and the shop that sells the great dreamer rod. high lure speed, high luck, and a duplication passive that makes it a farming rod as much as a rarity rod. stage 7 — endgame+ access late-game sail shop rod great dreamer rod — 500,000 c$ passive extra fish on a repeating cycle"},{"u":"locations/underground-music-venue/","n":"Underground Music Venue","t":"Locations","h":"underground music venue locations where the mainstream rod progression stops. rod-progression guides that begin with “take agaric’s free fungal rod” end with “finish on the wingripper or the chrysalis rod from the underground music venue” — these are the last rods most accounts will ever need. stage 7 — endgame+ access hidden; late-game rods wingripper, chrysalis role the end of the standard rod ladder"},{"u":"locations/castaway-cliffs/","n":"Castaway Cliffs","t":"Locations","h":"castaway cliffs locations the current money meta. the elder moss ripper rod’s lurking mossjaw passive puts a guaranteed high-value mossy great gold cursed shark on your line on a roughly two-minute timer, which turns the cliffs into an income rate rather than a fishing spot. stage 8 — money meta access late-game sail rod elder moss ripper rod rate 2–4m c$/hr, or 15–25m with the elder moss ripper"},{"u":"locations/calm-zone/","n":"The Calm Zone","t":"Locations","h":"the calm zone locations the other half of the endgame money meta, and the one that does not depend on owning a specific rod. its draw is the crystallized seadragon at roughly 26,100 c$ a catch on average — enough that a good session here funds an entire rod tier. stage 8 — money meta access deep water; endgame rod required money fish crystallized seadragon — ~26,100 c$ average prerequisite a rod that can land deep-water weight"},{"u":"locations/brine-pool/","n":"The Brine Pool","t":"Locations","h":"the brine pool locations one of the two hazard pools — the brine pool and the roslit volcano — that ordinary rods cannot fish. the exalted invincible enchant removes the restriction outright for whatever rod carries it, which is most of why it is chased. stage 8 access hazard water requires invincible enchant, or a rod built for it sibling hazard roslit volcano"},{"u":"locations/fischfest/","n":"Fischfest","t":"Locations","h":"fischfest locations fisch’s recurring festival hub. event locations carry their own bestiary blocks and their own rods, and they close on a schedule — a fischfest rod you did not buy while the gate was open is not purchasable afterwards. stage 9 — event access open while the event runs 2026 window closed 12 september 2026 holds event bestiary, crates, seasonal rods"},{"u":"locations/skycrest/","n":"Skycrest","t":"Locations","h":"skycrest locations the floating island above fischfest, added on 5 september 2026 and closed a week later with the festival. it is the clearest example of fisch’s modern event design: a self-contained progression track with its own currency, its own gear and a boss at the end. stage 9 — event added 5 september 2026 window 5–12 september 2026 access from fischfest, head right into the sea and swim up the waterfall progression crest amulet → idol favor → 10 sky crystals → abaia’s chamber bestiary 29 fish"},{"u":"locations/marianas-veil/","n":"Mariana&#8217;s Veil","t":"Locations","h":"mariana’s veil locations the deep-water expansion, and the single most important update for anyone chasing gear: it added five rods, and two of them — the ethereal prism rod and the rod of the zenith — sit at the very top of current tier lists. stage 8 added mariana’s veil update rods volcanic, challenger’s, rod of the zenith, ethereal prism, leviathan’s fang sub-areas volcanic vents, challenger deep, abyssal zenith, rainbow lake, veil of the forsaken boss scylla"},{"u":"locations/challenger-deep/","n":"Challenger Deep","t":"Locations","h":"challenger deep locations the deepest point in fisch, and the shop for the challenger’s rod. its +20% reeling progress speed is the sort of passive that sounds dull and turns into a permanent raise on every money farm you ever run. stage 8 part of mariana’s veil coordinates around 740, −3355, −1530 rod challenger’s rod — 2,500,000 c$"},{"u":"locations/abyssal-zenith/","n":"Abyssal Zenith","t":"Locations","h":"abyssal zenith locations home of the only rod in fisch that pays you for playing the minigame well. perfect catches build a mutation streak; one miss resets it. stage 8 part of mariana’s veil coordinates southwest of the pool, around −13625, −11035, −355 rod rod of the zenith — 10,000,000 c$"},{"u":"locations/sunken-depths/","n":"The Sunken Depths","t":"Locations","h":"the sunken depths locations a deep zone with its own trial chain and its own rod shelf. it is also where a weak rod stops being a handicap and becomes a hard stop: down here the species outweigh anything from the early game. stage 6 gate the sunken trials rods tempest rod, sunken rod, leviathan’s fang watch out for weight ceilings — deep species are heavy"},{"u":"locations/ancient-archives/","n":"The Ancient Archives","t":"Locations","h":"the ancient archives locations the crafting room, and the part of fisch that rewards planning instead of money. ten rods are craftable here, from mid-tier utility up to genuine endgame — and the room does not exist for you until the ancient isle totem puzzle is solved. stage 6 where inside ancient isle gate solve the ancient isle totem puzzle holds the rod crafting table craftable rods 10, plus requiem"},{"u":"locations/tidefall/","n":"Tidefall","t":"Locations","h":"tidefall locations one of the 2026 update zones, with its own secret rods, sub-zones and hunts. its fallen rod is the entry ticket the rest of the zone is balanced around. stage 7 added tidefall update entry rod fallen rod holds secret rods, sub-zones and hunts"},{"u":"locations/scoria-reach/","n":"Scoria Reach","t":"Locations","h":"scoria reach locations a volcanic update zone released in version 1.71.0. it sits in the same family as the volcanic vents and the ashen fortune mutation — heat-flavoured content with its own bestiary block. stage 7 added version 1.71.0, march 2026 flavour volcanic related volcanic rod, ashen fortune"},{"u":"mechanics/crafting/","n":"Rod crafting","t":"Mechanics","h":"rod crafting mechanics the route to a strong rod that does not run through your bank balance. ten rods are craftable at the ancient archives, each with its own level gate and three ingredients — and the ingredients are where the work is. where the ancient archives gate the ancient isle totem puzzle each recipe a level requirement and three ingredients catch some ingredients need a specific rod or mutation"},{"u":"mechanics/rod-mastery/","n":"Rod Mastery","t":"Mechanics","h":"rod mastery mechanics rods in fisch are not finished when you buy them. rod mastery attaches a quest set to individual rods, and clearing those quests permanently improves the rod as well as paying out cosmetics, c$ and xp. what a quest set attached to individual rods rewards passive boosts to the rod, c$, xp, skins, bobbers, lanterns, titles, halos, boots, gliders related the rod journal, and the masterline rod"},{"u":"rods/flimsy-rod/","n":"Flimsy Rod","t":"Rods","h":"flimsy rod rods every account starts with the flimsy rod and roughly no money. it is not good and it is not supposed to be — it exists to catch enough trash and common fish off the moosewood dock to pay for the carbon rod. stage 0 — start cost free — you start with it source given at spawn tier d role the rod you are handed"},{"u":"rods/training-rod/","n":"Training Rod","t":"Rods","h":"training rod rods a marginal step above the flimsy rod — slightly better control and resilience, still very low luck and weight. sold early enough that new players buy it before they know better, and every progression guide says the same thing: skip it. stage 0 — start cost 300 c$ source marc’s shop, moosewood tier d role skip it"},{"u":"rods/plastic-rod/","n":"Plastic Rod","t":"Rods","h":"plastic rod rods the first rod that looks like a real purchase at 900 c$, which is why so many accounts own it. it beats the flimsy rod and is still a bad buy, because the rod you actually want costs 2,000. stage 0 — start cost 900 c$ source marc’s shop, moosewood tier d role also skip it"},{"u":"rods/carbon-rod/","n":"Carbon Rod","t":"Rods","h":"carbon rod rods the consensus best beginner rod in fisch: balanced stats, a weight ceiling high enough for the early islands, and cheap enough to be your first real purchase rather than a project. buy it, then leave moosewood. stage 1 — early cost 2,000 c$ source marc’s shop, moosewood tier c role the first purchase worth making"},{"u":"rods/long-rod/","n":"Long Rod","t":"Rods","h":"long rod rods sold from a tent at moosewood rather than from marc’s shop, which is why plenty of players never find it. its selling point is casting distance — some species simply do not live where a short cast lands. stage 1 — early cost 3,000 c$ source beside a tent at moosewood tier c role reach, for the price of a snack"},{"u":"rods/fast-rod/","n":"Fast Rod","t":"Rods","h":"fast rod rods a lure-speed rod. fish bite sooner, so you get more casts per hour — worth real money when you are farming common fish for c$, worth much less when you are hunting one rare species. stage 1 — early cost 4,000 or 4,500 c$ source marc’s shop, moosewood tier c role casts per hour, not rarity"},{"u":"rods/lucky-rod/","n":"Lucky Rod","t":"Rods","h":"lucky rod rods the early luck rod. where the fast rod gives you more casts, the lucky rod makes each cast likelier to produce something rare — which is what fills a bestiary and what sells for more than pocket change. stage 1 — early cost 4,500 or 5,250 c$ source marc’s shop, moosewood tier c role rarity bias, early"},{"u":"rods/steady-rod/","n":"Steady Rod","t":"Rods","h":"steady rod rods the first rod that feels like equipment rather than a starter item. it widens the shake ui and carries enough control and resilience to land almost anything the early and early-mid islands throw at you. stage 1 — early cost 7,000 c$ source beside alfie, roslit hamlet tier b role the rod that ends the early game"},{"u":"rods/fungal-rod/","n":"Fungal Rod","t":"Rods","h":"fungal rod rods a free rod with a real passive, handed over for catching one alligator in the swamp. there is no other point in fisch where the reward-to-effort ratio is this lopsided, which is why every rod-progression guide routes through agaric. stage 2 — early-mid cost free source agaric, mushgrove swamp — catch an alligator tier b role the best value in the game"},{"u":"rods/stone-rod/","n":"Stone Rod","t":"Rods","h":"stone rod rods a 3,000 c$ rod sold on an island most players do not reach until the mid-game, which makes it an odd item: priced like a starter rod, stocked where nobody needs one. stage 4 — mid-late cost 3,000 c$ source ancient isle tier c role cheap, and a long way from home"},{"u":"rods/nocturnal-rod/","n":"Nocturnal Rod","t":"Rods","h":"nocturnal rod rods a cheap vertigo purchase built around the night cycle. fisch gates a real share of its species and mutations behind time of day, and this is the rod that specialises in the dark half. stage 5 — late cost 15,000 c$ source vertigo tier b role night fishing"},{"u":"rods/magnet-rod/","n":"Magnet Rod","t":"Rods","h":"magnet rod rods sold at terrapin island alongside the shipwright. a magnet rod pulls metal and junk out of the water, which sounds like a downside until you want the things that come with it. stage 1 — early cost 15,000 c$ source terrapin island tier b role junk, on purpose"},{"u":"rods/phoenix-rod/","n":"Phoenix Rod","t":"Rods","h":"phoenix rod rods the better of the two rods sold on ancient isle, at 40,000 c$. a reasonable purchase if you are already parked there farming enchant relics and have money spare. stage 4 — mid-late cost 40,000 c$ source ancient isle tier b role the ancient isle mid-tier buy"},{"u":"rods/midas-rod/","n":"Midas Rod","t":"Rods","h":"midas rod rods the dedicated money rod of the mid-game: a large chance for anything you catch to come up golden, doubling what it sells for. it does nothing for bestiary work and everything for your bank balance. stage 3 — mid cost 55,000 c$ source the travelling merchant tier b role a money rod, not a rarity rod"},{"u":"rods/aurora-rod/","n":"Aurora Rod","t":"Rods","h":"aurora rod rods bought in vertigo, but only while an aurora borealis is running — a shop that is only open in the right weather. it lets you catch fish carrying the aurora mutation. stage 5 — late cost 70,000 c$ source vertigo, during an aurora borealis tier b role a mutation you can farm"},{"u":"rods/kings-rod/","n":"King&#8217;s Rod","t":"Rods","h":"king’s rod rods not really a shop rod: it sits next to a skeleton in the keepers altar, directly left of the elevator as you come down. players who never paid the 400 c$ bribe have walked past it for months without knowing. stage 4 — mid-late cost 100,000 or 120,000 c$ source keepers altar — beside a skeleton, left of the elevator tier b role hidden in plain sight"},{"u":"rods/arctic-rod/","n":"Arctic Rod","t":"Rods","h":"arctic rod rods the standard buy between the free fungal rod and the trident rod. progression guides name it by position rather than by stat line: it is the rod you take north. stage 4 — mid-late cost shop price varies source northern summit tier b role the cold-biome step"},{"u":"rods/trident-rod/","n":"Trident Rod","t":"Rods","h":"trident rod rods the rod the mid-game is built around, and the first one that partly pays for itself. good at everything, exceptional at nothing, and carrying a passive that turns ordinary catches into triple-value ones. stage 4 — mid-late cost 150,000 c$ source trident’s temple tier a role the most flexible mid-game rod"},{"u":"rods/volcanic-rod/","n":"Volcanic Rod","t":"Rods","h":"volcanic rod rods one of the five rods added with mariana’s veil, and the cheapest genuinely strong money rod in the game. bought at the volcanic vents pool rather than from any town. stage 5 — late cost 150,000 c$ source volcanic vents pool — around 3180, −2035, 4020 tier a role a 5× mutation on a fifth of your catches"},{"u":"rods/destiny-rod/","n":"Destiny Rod","t":"Rods","h":"destiny rod rods cheap for its tier and locked behind work rather than money: caleia will not sell it until your total bestiary completion reaches 70%. it is the reward for having filled the easy locations properly on the way through. stage 5 — late cost 190,000 c$ source caleia, the arch — needs 70% bestiary tier a role the collection payoff"},{"u":"rods/leviathans-fang-rod/","n":"Leviathan&#8217;s Fang Rod","t":"Rods","h":"leviathan’s fang rod rods a mariana’s veil rod that has to be earned before it can be bought: the scylla boss fight gates the purchase. everything about it is aimed at the reeling minigame rather than at what bites. stage 6 — endgame cost 350,000 or 1,850,000 c$ source near the entrance to the veil of the forsaken — after the scylla fight tier a role fight-winning, not luck-winning"},{"u":"rods/great-dreamer-rod/","n":"Great Dreamer Rod","t":"Rods","h":"great dreamer rod rods powerful lure speed, high luck and a duplication passive, for 500,000 c$ — less than the rod of the depths and arguably ahead of it. if cursed isle is reachable for you, this is the better buy. stage 7 — endgame+ cost 500,000 c$ source cursed isle tier s role farming and rarity at once"},{"u":"rods/tempest-rod/","n":"Tempest Rod","t":"Rods","h":"tempest rod rods sold in the sunken depths behind the sunken trials. the two published prices differ by more than a million c$, which usually means a patch moved it — budget the higher one. stage 6 — endgame cost 500,000 or 1,850,000 c$ source sunken depths — after the sunken trials tier a role storm-water specialist"},{"u":"rods/rod-of-the-depths/","n":"Rod of the Depths","t":"Rods","h":"rod of the depths rods the rod most accounts carry from the late game into the endgame, and the reason players grind the entire vertigo bestiary. it costs 750,000 c$ and sits behind a key that cannot be bought. stage 5 — late cost 750,000 c$ source inside the depths tier a role the late-game workhorse"},{"u":"rods/abyssal-specter-rod/","n":"Abyssal Specter Rod","t":"Rods","h":"abyssal specter rod rods the entry-level purchase among the atlantis rods at 850,000 c$ — well under the poseidon, zeus and kraken rods sold on the same island. stage 6 — endgame cost 850,000 c$ source atlantis tier a role the cheapest atlantis rod"},{"u":"rods/kraken-rod/","n":"Kraken Rod","t":"Rods","h":"kraken rod rods an atlantis purchase gated on the kraken pool and on character level as well as money. rare-catch bias, a duplication effect and a tentacle surge make it the bridge between late-game farming and genuine endgame gear. stage 6 — endgame cost 950,000 or 1,333,333 c$ source atlantis — after unlocking the kraken pool, ~level 180 tier a role the endgame bridge"},{"u":"rods/poseidon-rod/","n":"Poseidon Rod","t":"Rods","h":"poseidon rod rods one of the three trial rods sold in atlantis. the money is the easy half; the poseidon trial is the half that decides when you get it. stage 6 — endgame cost 1,555,555 c$ source atlantis — after the poseidon trial tier a role trial-gated atlantis power"},{"u":"rods/zeus-rod/","n":"Zeus Rod","t":"Rods","h":"zeus rod rods sold at zeus’ rod room once the zeus trial is complete. at 1.7m c$ it is the most expensive of the standard atlantis rods. stage 6 — endgame cost 1,700,000 c$ source atlantis — after the zeus trial, at zeus’ rod room tier a role the other atlantis trial rod"},{"u":"rods/challengers-rod/","n":"Challenger&#8217;s Rod","t":"Rods","h":"challenger’s rod rods a mariana’s veil rod bought in the deepest water in the game. its passive is unglamorous and quietly excellent. stage 8 — money meta cost 2,500,000 c$ source challenger deep — around 740, −3355, −1530 tier s role faster fights, forever"},{"u":"rods/heavens-rod/","n":"Heaven&#8217;s Rod","t":"Rods","h":"heaven’s rod rods hidden behind a puzzle in a cave near the top of northern summit, and then sold for 2,750,000 c$. two separate walls, one after the other. stage 4 — mid-late cost 2,750,000 c$ source northern summit — solve the cave puzzle first tier s role a puzzle, then a price tag"},{"u":"rods/chrysalis-rod/","n":"Chrysalis Rod","t":"Rods","h":"chrysalis rod rods one of the two rods the mainstream progression guides finish on. past this point the ladder stops being a ladder and becomes a question of which specialist rod suits what you are farming. stage 7 — endgame+ cost not a plain shop purchase source underground music venue tier s role end of the standard ladder"},{"u":"rods/wingripper-rod/","n":"Wingripper Rod","t":"Rods","h":"wingripper rod rods the other finisher from the underground music venue, and the other correct answer to “what is the last rod i need”. interchangeable with the chrysalis for most purposes, and a fixture near the top of every tier list. stage 7 — endgame+ cost not a plain shop purchase source underground music venue tier s role end of the standard ladder"},{"u":"rods/elder-moss-ripper/","n":"Elder Moss Ripper Rod","t":"Rods","h":"elder moss ripper rod rods the rod that defines endgame income. its lurking mossjaw passive guarantees a high-value mossy great gold cursed shark on roughly a two-minute cycle, which is why castaway cliffs is quoted at 15–25m c$ per hour with it and 2–4m without. stage 8 — money meta cost castaway cliffs — verify in game source castaway cliffs tier s role the money meta, single-handedly"},{"u":"rods/ethereal-prism-rod/","n":"Ethereal Prism Rod","t":"Rods","h":"ethereal prism rod rods named outright by tier lists as the single best rod in fisch, for one reason: money. the highest luck in the game, excellent lure speed, and a passive that fires on half of everything you catch. stage 8 — money meta cost 3,500,000 or 15,000,000 c$ source island in the middle of rainbow lake — needs the forsaken gate and the veil of the forsaken bestiary tier s role the best money rod in the game"},{"u":"rods/rod-of-the-zenith/","n":"Rod of the Zenith","t":"Rods","h":"rod of the zenith rods the mariana’s veil skill rod. it is the only rod in the game that asks you to be good at the minigame and pays you for it. stage 8 — money meta cost 10,000,000 c$ source abyssal zenith — southwest of the pool, around −13625, −11035, −355 tier s role rewards perfect play, literally"},{"u":"rods/requiem/","n":"Requiem","t":"Rods","h":"requiem rods the headline craft. fifteen million c$ is the easy part of the recipe; the four ingredients are the reason so few accounts carry one. stage 8 — money meta cost 15,000,000 c$ plus ingredients source crafted at the ancient archives tier s role the crafting endgame"},{"u":"rods/fabulous-rod/","n":"Fabulous Rod","t":"Rods","h":"fabulous rod rods awarded for finishing the final stage of the fabulous deity’s quest in the calm zone. you cannot even start it below level 1000. stage 8 — money meta cost quest reward — level 1000 source fabulous deity, calm zone tier s role a level-1000 wall"},{"u":"rods/masterline-rod/","n":"Masterline Rod","t":"Rods","h":"masterline rod rods described as the best all-rounder in the game and earned rather than bought: complete the bestiary and the rod journal. other sources describe the 100% bestiary reward as cosmetic and do not mention a rod, so treat this as a target rather than a plan. stage 8 — money meta cost completion reward — disputed source bestiary + rod journal completion tier s role the completionist rod"},{"u":"rods/olympian-godbreaker/","n":"Olympian Godbreaker","t":"Rods","h":"olympian godbreaker rods the top of the game. fifty million c$, level 981, a boss catch, and complete bestiaries — every gate fisch has, on one item. stage 8 — money meta cost 50,000,000 c$ source olympian fissure — level 981, after catching the olympian devil, with 100% bestiaries tier s role the hardest thing to own"},{"u":"rods/ruinous-oath/","n":"Ruinous Oath","t":"Rods","h":"ruinous oath rods named repeatedly when high-level players are asked what the best rod in fisch is: very high luck, very high lure speed, no meaningful weakness. stage 8 — money meta cost endgame acquisition source endgame content tier s role a high-level favourite"},{"u":"rods/resourceful-rod/","n":"Resourceful Rod","t":"Rods","h":"resourceful rod rods one of the ten rods craftable at the ancient archives. each craft has its own level requirement and three ingredients, and some of those ingredients have to be fished with a specific rod or carry a specific mutation before they count. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier b role craftable"},{"u":"rods/seasons-rod/","n":"Seasons Rod","t":"Rods","h":"seasons rod rods a craftable rod from the ancient archives. named for the seasonal conditions its ingredients and behaviour revolve around. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier b role craftable"},{"u":"rods/riptide-rod/","n":"Riptide Rod","t":"Rods","h":"riptide rod rods a craftable ancient archives rod. the archives themselves are the gate most players hit first: the room only opens after the ancient isle totem puzzle is solved. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier b role craftable"},{"u":"rods/voyager-rod/","n":"Voyager Rod","t":"Rods","h":"voyager rod rods a craftable rod that matters beyond its own stat line: the requiem recipe requires a fossilized plesiosaur caught with a voyager rod. you cannot substitute another rod for that line. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier a role craftable, and a prerequisite"},{"u":"rods/lost-rod/","n":"The Lost Rod","t":"Rods","h":"the lost rod rods a craftable ancient archives rod with its own documented page on the official wiki, which is more than most rods at this tier can claim. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier b role craftable"},{"u":"rods/celestial-rod/","n":"Celestial Rod","t":"Rods","h":"celestial rod rods one of the stronger ancient archives crafts. celestial and night-cycle content overlap in fisch, so it pairs naturally with a sundial totem. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier a role craftable"},{"u":"rods/rod-of-the-eternal-king/","n":"Rod of the Eternal King","t":"Rods","h":"rod of the eternal king rods the craftable rod that shows up in tier lists next to rods costing millions. fisch’s crafting system is not a side activity — its ceiling is genuinely endgame. stage 7 — endgame+ cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier s role craftable, and top-tier"},{"u":"rods/rod-of-the-forgotten-fang/","n":"Rod of the Forgotten Fang","t":"Rods","h":"rod of the forgotten fang rods an ancient archives craft. named alongside the eternal king and the spiritbinder as the upper end of what the crafting table produces. stage 7 — endgame+ cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier a role craftable"},{"u":"rods/spiritbinder/","n":"Spiritbinder","t":"Rods","h":"spiritbinder rods one of the ten ancient archives crafts, and one of the better-regarded ones. stage 7 — endgame+ cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier a role craftable"},{"u":"rods/vineweaver-rod/","n":"Vineweaver Rod","t":"Rods","h":"vineweaver rod rods a craftable ancient archives rod, on the swamp-and-overgrowth end of the roster. stage 6 — endgame cost crafted — level gate + 3 ingredients source ancient archives tier b role craftable"},{"u":"rods/fallen-rod/","n":"Fallen Rod","t":"Rods","h":"fallen rod rods described as the first essential rod of the tidefall content. update zones in fisch usually ship with one rod that is effectively the entry ticket to the rest of the zone, and this is tidefall’s. stage 7 — endgame+ cost tidefall — verify in game source tidefall tier a role the tidefall starter"},{"u":"rods/ancient-idol-rod/","n":"Ancient Idol Rod","t":"Rods","h":"ancient idol rod rods a skycrest event rod earned rather than bought: collect all seven ancient idol charms and catch five giant fish at skycrest, then hand them to forge master torin. stage 9 — event cost quest — 7 ancient idol charms + 5 giant fish source forge master torin, skycrest tier s role 165% luck, infinite weight"},{"u":"rods/fruitline/","n":"Fruitline","t":"Rods","h":"fruitline rods the other skycrest headline rod, and the luck record-holder: 200% luck with infinite max weight. limited-time, and a genuine chain of work to get. stage 9 — event cost quest — fruit lover frank, then the fruity abaia source skycrest tier s role the highest luck of any rod"},{"u":"rods/migu-rod/","n":"MiguRod","t":"Rods","h":"migurod rods one of the rods september 2026 tier lists lead with. its acquisition route is not consistently written up anywhere this wiki could check, so it is listed by name rather than described in detail. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier s role tier-list regular"},{"u":"rods/castbound/","n":"Castbound","t":"Rods","h":"castbound rods a rod named among the top performers in current tier lists. documented here by name and standing; its route is not something this wiki can confirm. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier s role tier-list regular"},{"u":"rods/polaris-serenade/","n":"Polaris Serenade","t":"Rods","h":"polaris serenade rods one half of a pair with the astraeus serenade, both named in the upper tiers of current lists. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier s role tier-list regular"},{"u":"rods/astraeus-serenade/","n":"Astraeus Serenade","t":"Rods","h":"astraeus serenade rods grouped with the fabulous rod and hades’ soul-scythe as rods carrying 250–300% luck with solid control and resilience — the consistency picks for rare hunting at the top of the game. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier s role 250–300% luck band"},{"u":"rods/hades-soul-scythe/","n":"Hades&#8217; Soul-Scythe","t":"Rods","h":"hades’ soul-scythe rods named alongside the astraeus serenade and the fabulous rod in the 250–300% luck bracket. part of the olympus-flavoured content that also produced the olympian godbreaker. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier s role 250–300% luck band"},{"u":"rods/dreambreaker/","n":"Dreambreaker","t":"Rods","h":"dreambreaker rods a top-tier rod named in current lists, and presumably related to the great dreamer rod line — though nothing this wiki could check confirms that. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier s role tier-list regular"},{"u":"rods/cinderstring/","n":"Cinderstring","t":"Rods","h":"cinderstring rods a fire-flavoured rod named in the upper tiers, fitting the same family as the volcanic rod and the ashen fortune mutation. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier a role tier-list regular"},{"u":"rods/fang-of-the-eclipse/","n":"Fang of the Eclipse","t":"Rods","h":"fang of the eclipse rods an eclipse-themed rod named among the notable performers. eclipse and night content overlap, so it likely sits with the nocturnal rod family. stage 8 — money meta cost named in tier lists — verify in game source late-game content tier a role tier-list regular"},{"u":"rods/sunken-rod/","n":"Sunken Rod","t":"Rods","h":"sunken rod rods a rod tied to the sunken depths, alongside the tempest and leviathan’s fang rods. deep water is where weight ceilings and resilience start deciding outcomes. stage 6 — endgame cost sunken depths — verify in game source sunken depths tier a role deep-water specialist"},{"u":"rods/mythical-rod/","n":"Mythical Rod","t":"Rods","h":"mythical rod rods a long-standing rod in the fisch roster, built around chasing rarity rather than weight or speed. stage 6 — endgame cost verify in game source mid-late content tier a role rarity-focused"},{"u":"rods/apollos-sunshot/","n":"Apollo&#8217;s Sunshot","t":"Rods","h":"apollo’s sunshot rods part of the olympus-flavoured content, and connected to the solar mutation line that also runs through sunstone island. stage 8 — money meta cost verify in game source olympus content tier s role sun and solar content"},{"u":"rods/rod-of-the-singularity/","n":"Rod of the Singularity","t":"Rods","h":"rod of the singularity rods an endgame rod documented in dedicated guides. named here for completeness — the acquisition route is not something this wiki could confirm from the sources available to it. stage 8 — money meta cost verify in game source endgame content tier s role endgame oddity"},{"u":"rods/noiseform-rod/","n":"Noiseform Rod","t":"Rods","h":"noiseform rod rods earned through the shady bazaar questline, which runs three separate catch quests rather than asking for money. the same content line carries a chromatic skin code. stage 8 — money meta cost shady bazaar questline — three catch quests source shady bazaar tier a role questline rod"},{"u":"rods/lullaby/","n":"Lullaby","t":"Rods","h":"lullaby rods a named rod documented on the community wikis. included so the roster here is honest about the size of the game rather than tidy. stage 8 — money meta cost verify in game source late-game content tier a role named rod"},{"u":"baits/worm/","n":"Worm","t":"Baits","h":"worm baits the default bait. a small universal luck bump for almost nothing, which makes it the right thing to have on the line when you are farming volume rather than hunting a species. rarity common effect small universal luck sources starter bait; shops and bait spots everywhere"},{"u":"baits/fish-head/","n":"Fish Head","t":"Baits","h":"fish head baits the other everyday bait. interchangeable with the worm for most purposes — use whichever you have more of and save the good baits for when you are actually hunting something. rarity common effect small luck; cheap and plentiful sources shops, crates, cut from catches"},{"u":"baits/flakes/","n":"Flakes","t":"Baits","h":"flakes baits bulk bait. buy it in stacks when you are settling in for a long farming session, because running out of bait mid-session costs more than the bait does. rarity common effect small universal luck sources shops"},{"u":"baits/squid/","n":"Squid","t":"Baits","h":"squid baits the first bait that behaves like real equipment: it raises both preferred and universal luck at the cost of lure speed. you are trading casts per hour for quality per cast, which is the correct trade when you are filling a bestiary. rarity rare effect preferred and universal luck; lower lure speed sources caught, crates"},{"u":"baits/truffle-worm/","n":"Truffle Worm","t":"Baits","h":"truffle worm baits the species-hunting bait. a very large preferred-luck bonus for only a small lure-speed penalty — the best bait in the game for going after one specific fish, and close to wasted when you are farming whatever bites. rarity legendary effect +300% preferred luck, −10% lure speed sources crates, events, bait spots"},{"u":"baits/weird-algae/","n":"Weird Algae","t":"Baits","h":"weird algae baits the rarity-hunting bait. it biases the whole table upward rather than one species, and it costs a third of your casting speed to do it. right for bestiary sweeps and rare-drop farming, wrong for money farming, where throughput is the point. rarity legendary effect +200% universal luck, −35% lure speed sources crates, bait spots"},{"u":"fish/alligator/","n":"Alligator","t":"Fish","h":"alligator fish the most valuable fish in the early game and it sells for almost nothing. catching one alligator in mushgrove swamp completes agaric’s quest, and agaric hands over the fungal rod for free. rarity rare where mushgrove swamp why it matters agaric’s quest fish — catch one, get the fungal rod free"},{"u":"fish/nurse-shark/","n":"Nurse Shark","t":"Fish","h":"nurse shark fish not valuable in itself. it matters because the water where nurse sharks spawn in roslit bay is the early-game enchant relic farm — if you are catching them, you are in the right spot. rarity uncommon where roslit bay shallows why it matters marks the early enchant relic shallows"},{"u":"fish/colossal-squid/","n":"Colossal Squid","t":"Fish","h":"colossal squid fish one of the fish that will not appear until the weather cooperates. fog is the condition, and a smokescreen totem is how you make fog happen instead of waiting for it. rarity legendary where deep water, foggy weather why it matters a weather-gated bestiary entry"},{"u":"fish/crowned-anglerfish/","n":"Crowned Anglerfish","t":"Fish","h":"crowned anglerfish fish filed with the colossal squid for the same reason: fog-preferring, deep, and a bestiary hole that stays open for a long time if you never buy a totem. rarity legendary where deep water, foggy weather why it matters the other classic fog catch"},{"u":"fish/crystallized-seadragon/","n":"Crystallized Seadragon","t":"Fish","h":"crystallized seadragon fish the single fish the endgame money meta is built on outside the castaway cliffs setup. at roughly 26,100 c$ on average it turns a calm zone session into a rod budget. rarity mythical where the calm zone why it matters ~26,100 c$ average — the endgame money fish"},{"u":"fish/mossy-great-gold-cursed-shark/","n":"Mossy Great Gold Cursed Shark","t":"Fish","h":"mossy great gold cursed shark fish the fish behind the 15–25m c$/hr figure. the elder moss ripper rod’s lurking mossjaw passive puts one on your line roughly every two minutes, which is an income rate rather than a drop rate. rarity mythical where castaway cliffs why it matters the elder moss ripper’s guaranteed catch, ~every 2 min"},{"u":"fish/megalodon/","n":"Megalodon","t":"Fish","h":"megalodon fish the classic fisch trophy: an open-world hunt rather than a fish you find. servers force megalodon hunts through day/night cycling, which is why organised players carry stacks of sundial totems. rarity secret where open ocean — hunt event why it matters the open-world boss catch"},{"u":"fish/isonade/","n":"Isonade","t":"Fish","h":"isonade fish community write-ups reach for isonade whenever they explain stacking, because the canonical worked example is a glitched shiny sparkling big silver isonade — attributes and a mutation on one fish, all multiplying together. rarity mythical where deep water why it matters the standard example of a stacked catch"},{"u":"mutations/aether/","n":"Aether","t":"Mutations","h":"aether mutations the top standard mutation. rare enough that most players see one a handful of times. multiplier 12× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/tryhard/","n":"Tryhard","t":"Mutations","h":"tryhard mutations joint second among standard mutations. multiplier 10× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/plagued/","n":"Plagued","t":"Mutations","h":"plagued mutations joint second, and the one people most often mistake for a debuff. multiplier 10× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/atlantean/","n":"Atlantean","t":"Mutations","h":"atlantean mutations the trident rod applies it at roughly a 30% rate — the only mutation you can reliably manufacture mid-game. multiplier 3× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/midas/","n":"Midas","t":"Mutations","h":"midas mutations top of the common-tier multipliers, and the one the midas rod is named for. multiplier 2.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/purified/","n":"Purified","t":"Mutations","h":"purified mutations shares the 2.5× band with midas. multiplier 2.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/sleet/","n":"Sleet","t":"Mutations","h":"sleet mutations a cold-biome mutation — snowcap and the northern water. multiplier 2.4× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/electric/","n":"Electric","t":"Mutations","h":"electric mutations storm-adjacent. weather changes what you can roll. multiplier 2.1× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/aurelian/","n":"Aurelian","t":"Mutations","h":"aurelian mutations solid 2× band. multiplier 2× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/lightning/","n":"Lightning","t":"Mutations","h":"lightning mutations storm weather. a tempest totem makes storms happen on demand. multiplier 2× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/shiny/","n":"Shiny","t":"Mutations","h":"shiny mutations an attribute, not a mutation: admin-event only, stacks with a real mutation, and — critically — cannot be lost when you appraise. multiplier 1.85× value kind attribute (appraisal-safe) stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/sparkling/","n":"Sparkling","t":"Mutations","h":"sparkling mutations the other admin-event attribute. stacks with shiny and with a mutation on the same fish. multiplier 1.85× value kind attribute (appraisal-safe) stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/silver/","n":"Silver","t":"Mutations","h":"silver mutations common enough to see regularly on a farming session. multiplier 1.8× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/studded/","n":"Studded","t":"Mutations","h":"studded mutations shares the 1.8× band with silver. multiplier 1.8× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/glossy/","n":"Glossy","t":"Mutations","h":"glossy mutations mid-band, unremarkable, adds up over a session. multiplier 1.6× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/aurous/","n":"Aurous","t":"Mutations","h":"aurous mutations the 1.5× band is where most of your mutated catches land. multiplier 1.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/cement/","n":"Cement","t":"Mutations","h":"cement mutations 1.5× band. multiplier 1.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/darkened/","n":"Darkened","t":"Mutations","h":"darkened mutations 1.5× band; night-adjacent. multiplier 1.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/frozen/","n":"Frozen","t":"Mutations","h":"frozen mutations 1.5× band; cold water. multiplier 1.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/mosaic/","n":"Mosaic","t":"Mutations","h":"mosaic mutations 1.5× band. multiplier 1.5× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/subspace/","n":"Subspace","t":"Mutations","h":"subspace mutations applied by the exalted quantum enchant at a 25% rate. the enchant is the reliable source; the multiplier itself is not consistently published. multiplier not consistently published kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"mutations/golden/","n":"Golden","t":"Mutations","h":"golden mutations doubles value. the midas rod applies it at roughly 60%. multiplier 2× value kind mutation stacks with attributes, weight, and appraisal rerolls"},{"u":"enchants/quantum/","n":"Quantum","t":"Enchants","h":"quantum enchants the mutation-farming enchant. a quarter of everything you catch comes up mutated, which compounds with weight and attributes into sale values nothing else reaches. relic exalted effect 25% chance for a caught fish to gain the subspace mutation applied at keepers altar roll random from its pool"},{"u":"enchants/sea-overlord/","n":"Sea Overlord","t":"Enchants","h":"sea overlord enchants a flat 25% on weight, and weight is a direct multiplier on sale value — so this is a flat 25% raise on every fish you sell, forever, with no conditions attached. relic exalted effect +25% fish weight applied at keepers altar roll random from its pool"},{"u":"enchants/invincible/","n":"Invincible","t":"Enchants","h":"invincible enchants access rather than power. the two hazard pools reject ordinary rods; invincible removes the restriction for whatever rod carries it. relic exalted effect fish the brine pool and roslit volcano regardless of rod applied at keepers altar roll random from its pool"},{"u":"enchants/immortal/","n":"Immortal","t":"Enchants","h":"immortal enchants the all-rounder pick: good luck, good lure speed, no glaring weakness. named alongside quantum whenever players are asked for the best enchant in the game. relic pool disputed effect strong balance of luck and speed applied at keepers altar roll random from its pool"},{"u":"items/rowboat/","n":"Rowboat","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"rowboat items & gear the cheapest important purchase in fisch. without a boat there is one island; with one there is a game. buy it in your first session, before any rod above the carbon rod. kind boat source / effect 400 c$ from the shipwright at moosewood docks — the unlock that opens the map"},{"u":"items/enchant-relic/","n":"Enchant Relic","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"enchant relic items & gear the currency of enchanting. one relic buys one random enchant roll at the keepers altar, and since a new roll overwrites the old one, you want a stack before you start rather than one at a time. kind relic source / effect fished up — best at ancient isle, workable in roslit bay"},{"u":"items/exalted-relic/","n":"Exalted Relic","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"exalted relic items & gear rolls from a smaller pool of much stronger enchants — quantum, sea overlord, invincible. spend these on the rod you intend to keep, not the rod you happen to be holding. kind relic source / effect far rarer than a standard relic; same altar"},{"u":"items/depths-key/","n":"The Depths Key","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"the depths key items & gear the only way into the depths. it cannot be bought, traded around or skipped, and it will not drop at all until the vertigo bestiary is complete. kind key source / effect fished from the strange whirlpool in vertigo, after 100% vertigo bestiary"},{"u":"items/crest-amulet/","n":"Crest Amulet","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"crest amulet items & gear the skycrest amulet, and the socket that charms go into. everything on the island runs through it. kind event gear source / effect taken from the keeper of the sky on skycrest"},{"u":"items/sky-crystal/","n":"Sky Crystal","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"sky crystal items & gear collect and place all ten to open abaia’s chamber. the gate is completion, not luck — each crystal is findable. kind event item source / effect 10 of them, hidden around skycrest"},{"u":"items/charms/","n":"Charms","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"charms items & gear charms level up as you fish with them equipped, and a levelled charm’s passive is substantially stronger than a fresh one. pick one and commit rather than rotating. kind event gear source / effect nine skycrest charms, socketed into the crest amulet"},{"u":"items/totems/","n":"Totems","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"totems items & gear consumables that overwrite the server’s time and weather. this is the single most underused system in fisch: instead of waiting for the condition a fish wants, you buy it. kind consumable source / effect roughly 20–26 totems; shops, crates, codes"},{"u":"items/sundial-totem/","n":"Sundial Totem","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"sundial totem items & gear the time totem, and the backbone of organised megalodon hunting — players cycle day and night with 60–70 totems to force hunt events to spawn. kind totem source / effect cycles the server’s time of day"},{"u":"items/tempest-totem/","n":"Tempest Totem","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"tempest totem items & gear rain and storms gate a set of species and storm-band mutations such as lightning. one totem replaces an indefinite wait. kind totem source / effect forces rain"},{"u":"items/windset-totem/","n":"Windset Totem","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"windset totem items & gear wind is its own weather state with its own preferring species. cheap, specific, and the reason a stalled bestiary suddenly moves. kind totem source / effect forces windy weather"},{"u":"items/smokescreen-totem/","n":"Smokescreen Totem","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"smokescreen totem items & gear the fog totem — how you get the colossal squid and crowned anglerfish without camping the weather. kind totem source / effect forces fog"},{"u":"items/clearcast-totem/","n":"Clearcast Totem","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"clearcast totem items & gear the undo button. useful when someone else’s totem has put the server into weather you do not want. kind totem source / effect clears the weather"},{"u":"items/potions/","n":"Potions","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"potions items & gear timed stat boosts. the xp potion is the one that matters for levelling — a temporary xp boost stacked with everything else is how max-level runs are done. kind consumable source / effect four potions; shops and events"},{"u":"items/shell-of-wrath/","n":"Shell of Wrath","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"shell of wrath items & gear part of the standard xp-stacking loadout. xp bonuses in fisch stack from several unrelated sources, so collecting three small ones beats hunting for one big one. kind xp gear source / effect +25% xp"},{"u":"items/companions/","n":"Companions","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"companions items & gear companions are a stat slot, not a cosmetic. the xp-farming setups name a specific companion for a reason. kind companion source / effect pets that follow you and apply a passive — e.g. the relic construct"},{"u":"items/crates/","n":"Crates &amp; geodes","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"crates & geodes items & gear where most good bait actually comes from. if you are buying legendary bait rather than opening for it, you are overpaying. kind container source / effect bait crates, common and quality crates, coral and volcanic geodes, tropical crates"},{"u":"items/personal-aquarium/","n":"Personal Aquarium","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"personal aquarium items & gear a passive bait source and a place to store trophies instead of selling them. small, permanent, easy to forget you own. kind facility source / effect holds fish you keep; produces bait over time"},{"u":"items/harpoon-gun/","n":"Harpoon Gun","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"harpoon gun items & gear an alternative to the rod for some content, and significant enough that rod tier lists are dated “after the harpoon guns update”. treat any rod ranking written before it with suspicion. kind weapon source / effect added in the harpoon guns update"},{"u":"items/aurora-bobber/","n":"Aurora Bobber","t":"Items &amp; gear","h":"aurora bobber items & gear the completionist prize for a fully filled bestiary. sources name it differently, which is a good sign it is cosmetic rather than load-bearing. kind cosmetic reward source / effect 100% bestiary reward — name disputed"},{"u":"npcs/pierre/","n":"Pierre","t":"NPCs","h":"pierre npcs runs the tutorial. onboarding only — he is not a merchant and sells nothing. where moosewood beach role npc"},{"u":"npcs/marc/","n":"Marc","t":"NPCs","h":"marc npcs the starter rod shop: plastic, carbon, fast and lucky rods. the carbon rod at 2,000 c$ is the only one worth your first purchase. where moosewood role npc"},{"u":"npcs/moosewood-merchant/","n":"The Merchant","t":"NPCs","h":"the merchant npcs buys fish. every named island has one, so you are never far from selling. where moosewood, village centre role npc"},{"u":"npcs/shipwright/","n":"The Shipwright","t":"NPCs","h":"the shipwright npcs sells boats, starting with the rowboat at 400 c$. this is the npc that opens the map. where moosewood docks role npc"},{"u":"npcs/the-appraiser/","n":"The Appraiser","t":"NPCs","h":"the appraiser npcs re-rolls a fish’s weight and mutation for a fee — a second chance at a better variant without catching a new fish. where moosewood role npc"},{"u":"npcs/agaric/","n":"Agaric","t":"NPCs","h":"agaric npcs asks for one alligator and hands over the fungal rod free. the best-value npc in the game. where mushgrove swamp role npc"},{"u":"npcs/roslit-blacksmith/","n":"The Blacksmith","t":"NPCs","h":"the blacksmith npcs sells the steady rod — the rod that ends the early game. where roslit bay role npc"},{"u":"npcs/mine-guard/","n":"The Mine Guard","t":"NPCs","h":"the mine guard npcs takes a 400 c$ bribe and lets you down to the keepers altar. one-time, cheap, permanent. where statue of sovereignty, by the elevator role npc"},{"u":"npcs/caleia/","n":"Caleia","t":"NPCs","h":"caleia npcs sells the destiny rod for 190,000 c$ — but only once your total bestiary hits 70%. where the arch role npc"},{"u":"npcs/keeper-of-the-sky/","n":"Keeper of the Sky","t":"NPCs","h":"keeper of the sky npcs holds the crest amulet and takes the ten sky crystals that open abaia’s chamber. where skycrest role npc"},{"u":"npcs/merlin/","n":"Merlin","t":"NPCs","h":"merlin npcs sells enchant relics at 11,000 c$ and 10-minute luck vi boosts at 5,000 c$. xp-farming write-ups also credit him with a +20% xp boost. where sunstone island role npc"},{"u":"npcs/alfie/","n":"Alfie","t":"NPCs","h":"alfie npcs the steady rod sits beside him at 7,000 c$ — the rod that ends the early game. where roslit hamlet role npc"},{"u":"npcs/travelling-merchant/","n":"The Travelling Merchant","t":"NPCs","h":"the travelling merchant npcs stock and location both rotate. the midas rod at 55,000 c$ is his headline item, which is why guides disagree about where the midas rod comes from. where moves around role npc"},{"u":"npcs/forge-master-torin/","n":"Forge Master Torin","t":"NPCs","h":"forge master torin npcs takes seven ancient idol charms and five giant fish, and forges the ancient idol rod. where skycrest role npc"},{"u":"npcs/fruit-lover-frank/","n":"Fruit Lover Frank","t":"NPCs","h":"fruit lover frank npcs wants 25 tropical fruits, then a follow-up catch, then the fruity abaia — and pays out the fruitline, the highest-luck rod in the game. where skycrest role npc"},{"u":"bosses/megalodon-hunt/","n":"Megalodon Hunt","t":"Bosses &amp; hunts","h":"megalodon hunt bosses & hunts fisch’s signature hunt. it is a server event rather than a fishing spot, which is why the community answer to “how do i get a megalodon” is a stack of totems rather than a better rod. where open ocean how it starts forced by cycling the server’s day/night with ~60–70 sundial totems"},{"u":"bosses/kraken/","n":"The Kraken","t":"Bosses &amp; hunts","h":"the kraken bosses & hunts the base game’s most involved boss unlock. the pool does not exist for you until five hidden levers have been flicked. where kraken pool, beneath atlantis how it starts a five-lever world quest"},{"u":"bosses/abaia/","n":"Abaia","t":"Bosses &amp; hunts","h":"abaia bosses & hunts the skycrest event boss, and a good example of how modern fisch events are built: a currency to grind, a collection to finish, a weather condition to wait for, and a multi-stage fight at the end. where abaia’s chamber, beneath skycrest how it starts idol favor → 10 sky crystals → fire of spirits during a tropical squall"},{"u":"bosses/isonade-hunt/","n":"Isonade","t":"Bosses &amp; hunts","h":"isonade bosses & hunts treated as a trophy catch. its main appearance in the wikis is as the worked example of stacking — the fabled glitched shiny sparkling big silver isonade that every mutation explainer reaches for. where deep water how it starts a deep-water catch rather than a scripted quest"},{"u":"mechanics/minigame/","n":"The fishing minigame","t":"Mechanics","h":"the fishing minigame mechanics fisch’s core loop is three checks in a row, and each one is failed differently. most fish lost by new players are lost in the shake, not the reel. steps cast → shake → reel cast hold to fill the power meter, release shake click the prompts fast; a miss restarts the cast reel hold to move right, release to drift left"},{"u":"mechanics/luck/","n":"Luck &mdash; universal vs preferred","t":"Mechanics","h":"luck — universal vs preferred mechanics the most common gear mistake in fisch is stacking the wrong luck. universal luck raises your odds on everything; preferred luck raises your odds on something specific. a +300% preferred bait is close to worthless if you do not know what you are fishing for. universal luck biases the whole rarity table upward preferred luck boosts one species or a named set sources rod stat, bait, enchants, rod passives rule universal for sweeps, preferred for hunts"},{"u":"mechanics/lure-speed/","n":"Lure speed","t":"Mechanics","h":"lure speed mechanics lure speed decides how long you wait between bites, which makes it a throughput stat rather than a quality one. it is worth the most when the thing you are farming is common and the thing you want is volume. raises throughput trades against luck, on most baits matters most money farming and timer-based rod passives"},{"u":"mechanics/control/","n":"Control","t":"Mechanics","h":"control mechanics control is the difference between the reeling bar going where you meant and going where you pushed it. cheap rods have little of it, which is why hard catches feel unfair on a flimsy rod and routine on a steady rod. affects the reeling minigame high control bar responds precisely; less overshoot low control sloppy, drifty bar on hard fish"},{"u":"mechanics/resilience/","n":"Resilience","t":"Mechanics","h":"resilience mechanics resilience is your margin for error. with enough of it a fumbled reel costs progress; without it, the same fumble costs the catch. it is the least glamorous rod stat and the one that most changes how the game feels. affects failure tolerance in the reel high resilience mistakes cost progress, not the fish boosted by rod stats and some baits"},{"u":"mechanics/max-weight/","n":"Max weight","t":"Mechanics","h":"max weight mechanics a hard ceiling, not a soft one. deep-water and boss-tier species outweigh early rods outright, which is why the answer to “why can i never land anything here” is usually the rod rather than the technique. hard limit yes — over it, you do not land the fish raised by better rods weight also multiplies sale value"},{"u":"mechanics/rarity/","n":"Rarity tiers","t":"Mechanics","h":"rarity tiers mechanics rarity does two things at once: it decides how often a species appears and how hard its minigame is. the exact ladder is one of the messier parts of the fisch documentation — different community databases count 12, 17 or 18 tiers. tiers 12 to 18, depending on the source common chain trash · common · uncommon · unusual · rare · exotic · legendary · mythical · secret side categories limited, special, extinct effect higher tier → harder minigame, better value"},{"u":"mechanics/bestiary/","n":"The Bestiary","t":"Mechanics","h":"the bestiary mechanics fisch’s collection log, and the only system in the game that converts patience directly into gear. two thresholds actually matter: 70% total for the destiny rod, and 100% of vertigo for the depths key. tracked per location, and as a total 70% total destiny rod unlocks at caleia, 190,000 c$ 100% vertigo required before the depths key can drop 100% total reward name disputed"},{"u":"mechanics/appraisal/","n":"Appraisal","t":"Mechanics","h":"appraisal mechanics a second roll of the dice on a fish you already own. the appraiser re-rolls weight and mutation, which means it can improve a catch and can also ruin one — the mutation you have is not protected. npc the appraiser, moosewood re-rolls weight and mutation safe attributes — shiny, sparkling — are never lost risk a good mutation can be re-rolled into a worse one"},{"u":"mechanics/weather/","n":"Time &amp; weather","t":"Mechanics","h":"time & weather mechanics weather and time of day are not scenery in fisch — they decide what is catchable. the important consequence is that a stalled bestiary is usually a weather problem, and weather is purchasable. states day/night, rain, storm, wind, fog, clear, and event weather gates species availability and some mutations control totems overwrite the server state night carries its own xp and species effects"},{"u":"mechanics/xp/","n":"Levels &amp; XP","t":"Mechanics","h":"levels & xp mechanics the xp curve is arithmetic, not exponential, for the first thousand levels: each level costs 190 × your current level. that makes the early climb fast and the back half enormous — 997 million xp to reach the 2,000 cap. xp to next level 190 × current level level 1 → 2 190 xp past level 1001 doubles every 500 levels max level 2,000 total to max 997,120,000 xp gates locations, rods and gear — e.g. kraken rod at ~180"},{"u":"mechanics/money/","n":"C$ and selling","t":"Mechanics","h":"c$ and selling mechanics a fish’s price is its species’ base value multiplied by weight, then by whatever mutation and attributes it carries. every one of those terms is something you can influence, which is why two players fishing the same spot can earn ten times differently. currency c$ sold to the merchant on any island multipliers weight, mutations, attributes, appraisal endgame rates 2–4m/hr, or 15–25m/hr with the elder moss ripper"},{"u":"mechanics/boats/","n":"Boats","t":"Mechanics","h":"boats mechanics boats are how fisch does map unlocking: sail far enough from shore and island names appear above their locations, and visiting one is what unlocks it. there is no quest gate on most islands — only distance. first boat rowboat — 400 c$, moosewood docks what they do travel; island names reveal as you approach upgrades faster hulls sold as you progress"},{"u":"mechanics/enchant-system/","n":"Enchanting","t":"Mechanics","h":"enchanting mechanics fisch’s only rod-upgrade system that is not a purchase. you offer a relic at the keepers altar and get a random enchant, overwriting whatever the rod carried before. where keepers altar, under the statue of sovereignty entry 400 c$ bribe, once input enchant relic or exalted relic result a random enchant, replacing the current one"},{"u":"mechanics/bonuses/","n":"Gamepasses &amp; party bonuses","t":"Mechanics","h":"gamepasses & party bonuses mechanics two multipliers that have nothing to do with fishing: the double xp gamepass, and simply having friends in your party. five friends is +50% xp for no gear, no grinding and no cost. double xp gamepass — flat permanent xp multiplier friends +10% xp each, up to +50% with five stacks with everything else in the xp stack"},{"u":"locations/","n":"Locations","t":"Index","h":"locations index list all"},{"u":"npcs/","n":"NPCs","t":"Index","h":"npcs index list all"},{"u":"bosses/","n":"Bosses &amp; hunts","t":"Index","h":"bosses & hunts index list all"},{"u":"rods/","n":"Rods","t":"Index","h":"rods index list all"},{"u":"baits/","n":"Baits","t":"Index","h":"baits index list all"},{"u":"enchants/","n":"Enchants","t":"Index","h":"enchants index list all"},{"u":"items/","n":"Items &amp; gear","t":"Index","h":"items & gear index list all"},{"u":"fish/","n":"Fish","t":"Index","h":"fish index list all"},{"u":"mutations/","n":"Mutations","t":"Index","h":"mutations index list all"},{"u":"mechanics/","n":"Mechanics","t":"Index","h":"mechanics index list all"},{"u":"guides/beginner/","n":"Beginner&#8217;s guide","t":"Guide","h":"beginner’s guide guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/mistakes/","n":"12 beginner mistakes","t":"Guide","h":"12 beginner mistakes guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/money-guide/","n":"Making money","t":"Guide","h":"making money guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/xp-guide/","n":"XP &amp; levelling","t":"Guide","h":"xp & levelling guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/enchanting/","n":"Enchanting","t":"Guide","h":"enchanting guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/codes/","n":"Codes","t":"Guide","h":"codes guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/sources/","n":"Accuracy &amp; sources","t":"Guide","h":"accuracy & sources guide walkthrough"},{"u":"guides/progression/","n":"Progression roadmap","t":"Guide","h":"progression roadmap guide walkthrough"},{"u":"tools/path-planner/","n":"Where am I? &mdash; path planner","t":"Tool","h":"where am i? — path planner tool calculator planner"},{"u":"tools/rod-budget/","n":"Rod budget planner","t":"Tool","h":"rod budget planner tool calculator planner"},{"u":"tools/odds/","n":"Drop &amp; catch odds","t":"Tool","h":"drop & catch odds tool calculator planner"},{"u":"tools/fish-value/","n":"Fish value calculator","t":"Tool","h":"fish value calculator tool calculator planner"}];
